 "titulo": "Someone climbed my tower for the shift change 😰 Part 2 #horror #shorts",
 "capa": "THERE IS NO SHIFT CHANGE",
 "descripcion": "Tower Six knew Cal's name. Dispatch says there is no tower on that ridge. And someone is climbing his stairs.\n\n> Part 3: {when_next}.\nWould you open the floor?\n\nNarrated fiction. New part every day.\n#horror #horrorstories #scarystories #survival #creepypasta",
 "lineas": [
  {
   "texto": "Tower Six knew my name. I never say my name on the radio.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "So I called dispatch, on the real channel.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "The night operator said there's no tower on that ridge. Just a burned floor.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "Then she paused. Cal, who else is up there with you?",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "I said nobody. She said she could hear someone breathing on my microphone.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "I turned around. The room was empty. Of course it was.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "At 3:20, the light on the ridge was gone.",
   "pausa": 0.7
  },
  {
   "texto": "There was a lantern on the trail below my tower instead. Moving. Climbing.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "Rule one. Log every light. My hand shook so hard I could barely write.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "The radio clicked again. Radio check, Tower Nine. I'm coming up for the shift change.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "There is no shift change. Nobody relieves me for twenty-eight more days.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "My tower has ninety-two steps. I started counting the footsteps.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "Fifty. Sixty. Seventy. Slow and heavy, like an old man.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "At step eighty, the footsteps stopped.",
   "pausa": 0.9
  },
  {
   "texto": "Then someone knocked on the trapdoor in my floor.",
   "pausa": 0.9
  },
  {
   "texto": "Part three, {when_next}.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  }
 ],
